--  Generated by check.py from docs/diagnostics.md.  Do not edit;
--  regenerate with python3 check.py --catalogue.

package body Landin.Diagnostics.Explanations is

   LF : constant Character := Character'Val (10);

   function Explanation (Of_Code : Catalogue.Code_Name) return String
     is (case Of_Code is
            when Catalogue.No_Frontend =>
               "Retired. A source was read and no frontend was wired to "
               & "the driver. The frontend has been wired since the first "
               & "executable slice, so nothing raises this and the number "
               & "is kept so no other rule can take it.",
            when Catalogue.Unknown_Option =>
               "The command line asked for something the driver does not"
               & " define: an unknown option, an option without its value "
               & "or repeated where it may not be, or a combination the dr"
               & "iver refuses, such as `--emit` with no source, an output"
               & " that would overwrite a source or another output, or `re"
               & "fine explain` with a code no catalogue row holds. `refin"
               & "e --help` lists the options. The status is 2, which says"
               & " the request and not a program was wrong."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "An option that belongs to a command is written after it."
               & " One written before its command, or with no command at a"
               & "ll, is refused naming the commands it belongs to and whe"
               & "re it goes, as it was written: `refine --root=lib compil"
               & "e main.ldn` is told `refine compile --root=lib ...`, and"
               & " `refine -o x.s main.ldn` that `-o x.s` is an option of "
               & "`compile` (D384)."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "Give `--target=` only once. Repeating it is a misuse eve"
               & "n when both names are the same; the driver does not choo"
               & "se between target selections."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "`--toolchain=NAME` and `--linker=NAME` require `--emit=e"
               & "xe`: checking and assembly emission do not run a linker."
               & " They are also incompatible with `--help` and `--identif"
               & "y`, which do not compile. Each selection must have a non"
               & "empty value and may be given only once."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "`--link=static|libc` chooses how a hosted executable is "
               & "linked, and under `refine check` which C runtime the pro"
               & "gram is checked with; `static` needs a Linux target, and"
               & " a target with no hosted system takes neither. `check` t"
               & "akes `--firmware-entry` and `--build-report` as `compile"
               & "` does, and refuses an entry that names no firmware rout"
               & "ine (D383).",
            when Catalogue.Unreadable_Source =>
               "A source named on the command line is missing or cannot "
               & "be read. Check the path and its permissions.",
            when Catalogue.Unknown_Target =>
               "`--target=` names no target the compiler describes, or n"
               & "one was named and this compiler's own host is not a desc"
               & "ribed target, so a build has nothing to compile for unti"
               & "l one is named. `refine --identify` lists the described "
               & "targets.",
            when Catalogue.Unwritable_Output =>
               "An output file cannot be written, or `refine fmt` cannot"
               & " rewrite its input. For emitted output, check that the d"
               & "estination directory exists and is writable, or choose a"
               & "nother path with `-o`."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "Formatting writes into the file it read, so it needs a w"
               & "ritable ordinary file and, for the copy of the original "
               & "it keeps until the new bytes last, write permission in t"
               & "he file's directory (D358). The diagnostic names what it"
               & " met: a read-only file, a directory that refuses the cop"
               & "y, a set-user-ID or set-group-ID bit the caller could no"
               & "t set again, a Linux file with capabilities, or a write "
               & "that failed, and then whether the original bytes are bac"
               & "k or where their copy is kept. `refine fmt --stdout` pri"
               & "nts the layout without writing anything. See [formatter "
               & "file handling](format.md) for the full contract.",
            when Catalogue.Module_Not_Found =>
               "No import root holds the module an import names [1420]. "
               & "Roots are searched in the order `--root=` gives them, an"
               & "d a path's segments are directories under a root, spelle"
               & "d exactly; the note names every directory looked for, in"
               & " that order, so `import lexer/lexer` under `--root .` sa"
               & "ys it looked for `./lexer/lexer` (D384). When a director"
               & "y near the missing segment is there, the diagnostic offe"
               & "rs it as a likely fix; named files with no `--root` are "
               & "offered the library's `core`, `hosted` or `platform` whe"
               & "n the first segment is near one. An import of `core`, `h"
               & "osted` or `platform` when `refine` found no library besi"
               & "de itself, as a copied `refine` does not, names where it"
               & " looked; name the library's directory with `--library=DI"
               & "R` (D363).",
            when Catalogue.Module_Directory_Invalid =>
               "With `--root=`, the entry module is a readable directory"
               & " [1410], or the entry module's own source files, which a"
               & "re then one module as named files are without a root (D3"
               & "83). A path that is neither is refused. This code also r"
               & "eports an import root or intermediate directory that can"
               & "not be listed while searching in root order [1420]. Chec"
               & "k the named path and its permissions; a genuinely absent"
               & " module is reported by L0006.",
            when Catalogue.Module_Unavailable_For_Target =>
               "An import names a source namespace unavailable for the s"
               & "elected target (D267). `hosted/*` requires a hosted targ"
               & "et; `platform/c` requires one of the currently enabled L"
               & "P64 C ABIs; `platform/cortex_m` requires an M-profile ta"
               & "rget, including its higher supported feature levels. Sel"
               & "ect an applicable target or remove the import. Project-f"
               & "irst root selection cannot change namespace availability"
               & ".",
            when Catalogue.Root_Holds_Library_Module =>
               "A warning: an import of `core`, `hosted` or `platform` w"
               & "as read from the compiler's own library, and a `--root=`"
               & " directory also holds a module at that path, which was n"
               & "ot read (D275, D366). The library always supplies those "
               & "three namespaces, so a project's copy of `core` never re"
               & "places it. To compile against that copy instead, name it"
               & "s directory with `--library=DIR`; to silence the warning"
               & ", rename or remove the project's directory.",
            when Catalogue.Not_Formatted =>
               "`refine fmt --check` found a line that is not in the lay"
               & "out D252 decides and `docs/format.md` shows. There is on"
               & "e diagnostic for every such line, and its note shows the"
               & " line as the layout writes it, or says that the layout r"
               & "emoves the blank line or changes its line end (D359). A "
               & "line whose spacing changes is marked where it differs, f"
               & "rom the first byte the layout changes to the last, and t"
               & "he note names the column it differs from (D385). Nothing"
               & " is wrong with the program: run `refine fmt` on the file"
               & " to put it in the layout, which changes its space and no"
               & "thing else, or `refine fmt --stdout` to see the whole fi"
               & "le laid out.",
            when Catalogue.Unknown_Level =>
               "`--level=`, or the language server's `level` option, nam"
               & "es no CPU feature level of the selected target's family "
               & "(D255). A level belongs to one family, so `armv8.1-a` is"
               & " refused with `--target=linux-x86-64`, and synthetic-32 "
               & "has no level to select. `refine --identify` lists each t"
               & "arget's levels.",
            when Catalogue.Construct_Not_Enabled =>
               "The program uses a construct the tour describes and the "
               & "kernel does not enable yet [1830]. The two notes name th"
               & "e tour paragraph and whether the form is a recorded boun"
               & "dary, withdrawn with a replacement, or transferred to la"
               & "ter work. Write the program without it, or with what the"
               & " note says replaces it. A call's result is no place, so "
               & "indexing one is a recorded boundary: bind the result to "
               & "a name, then index the name.",
            when Catalogue.Malformed_Integer =>
               "An integer literal is malformed if a base prefix has no "
               & "digits, a digit is not in its base, an underscore begins"
               & " or ends the digit run, or the literal runs straight int"
               & "o a name [1770]. `0x` takes hexadecimal digits, `0b` bin"
               & "ary and `0o` octal. Keep underscores between digits, and"
               & " put a separator before a following name.",
            when Catalogue.Unknown_Bytes =>
               "A run of bytes no lexical rule spells [1750], or a word "
               & "with a capital in it. A name is lower case [1760], and a"
               & " byte outside the source alphabet belongs in a text lite"
               & "ral. A word of letters, digits and underscores that hold"
               & "s a capital is one report over the whole word, and the p"
               & "rogram is read on as if it were a name, so nothing else "
               & "is said about it; the note offers its lower-case spellin"
               & "g, `init_window` for `InitWindow`. A C function keeps C'"
               & "s spelling as its link symbol and takes a lower-case Lan"
               & "din name, which the note shows when the word names an `e"
               & "xtern(c)` function without one: `extern(c) link(symbol: "
               & """InitWindow"") init_window: ...` [1610] (D528).",
            when Catalogue.Unterminated_Comment =>
               "A block comment that is never closed [1780]. Every opene"
               & "r needs its closer; the second label shows where the com"
               & "ment began.",
            when Catalogue.Unterminated_Literal =>
               "An ordinary quoted text or character literal must close "
               & "before its line ends [0250] [0260]. A raw text literal m"
               & "ay span lines [0280]. Its maximal opening quote run sets"
               & " the delimiter width; only a later run of at least that "
               & "many quotes closes it. A shorter run remains content. Cl"
               & "ose the ordinary literal on its line, or add enough clos"
               & "ing quotes to the raw literal.",
            when Catalogue.Name_Expected =>
               "A name belongs here and something else stands there [176"
               & "0]. A keyword is never a name, including a control word "
               & "in any position (D225), and `_` alone is the discard. Ch"
               & "oose another name, such as `begin_value` for `begin`. A "
               & "keyword written as a binding's name is reported once, an"
               & "d its later uses as a value are the same mistake (D368)."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "A `match` arm that begins with a number names a value wh"
               & "ere a case belongs: compare values with `if` and `elsif`"
               & " (D369). Statements on the lines under a bare `else` wer"
               & "e meant as a recovery block, which binds the error first"
               & ": `else (problem)`, closed by `end` (D370). `_` among se"
               & "veral labels of one arm is refused too: it covers every "
               & "case no other arm names, so it is an arm of its own (D40"
               & "5).",
            when Catalogue.Type_Expected =>
               "A type position holds nothing the kernel enables as a ty"
               & "pe [1790].",
            when Catalogue.Expression_Expected =>
               "An expression was required and none begins here [1820]: "
               & "an operator with no operand, or a separator where a valu"
               & "e belongs.",
            when Catalogue.Token_Expected =>
               "A token the grammar requires is absent [1810]. The secon"
               & "d label points at the construct that required it. When a"
               & " name near the required keyword stands in its place, suc"
               & "h as `thne` for `then`, the diagnostic offers the keywor"
               & "d as a likely fix. An arm that names several cases binds"
               & " no payload, so bindings after them are refused here: gi"
               & "ve the case whose payload is bound an arm of its own (D4"
               & "05). Only a name is indexed [0570], so a text literal fo"
               & "llowed by `[` is refused with the route, a name given to"
               & " the text first; no repair removes the literal, which wo"
               & "uld change what the line computes. Nor is an applied typ"
               & "e called to make a value: `list(i32)(items: ..., len: 3)"
               & "` is refused naming the form that works, the fields in p"
               & "arentheses where the type is declared [1350].",
            when Catalogue.Unclosed_Construct =>
               "A construct opened and its `end` never arrived [1800]. T"
               & "he second label shows where it opened; close it there.",
            when Catalogue.Assignment_In_Expression =>
               "Assignment is a statement and never an expression [0390]"
               & ". `==` compares. When the assignment is an `=`, the diag"
               & "nostic offers `==` as a likely fix.",
            when Catalogue.Comparison_Chained =>
               "A comparison takes at most one operator [1820]: `a < b <"
               & " c` compares a `bool` with `c`. Write `a < b and b < c`.",
            when Catalogue.Return_Carries_Value =>
               "`return` carries no value [1810]. Assign the named retur"
               & "n, then `return`.",
            when Catalogue.Public_On_Statement =>
               "`public` belongs on a module declaration and never on a "
               & "statement [1740].",
            when Catalogue.End_Name_Mismatch =>
               "The name after `end` must be the name of what it closes "
               & "[1800], or be absent where the construct allows that. Th"
               & "e diagnostic offers the declared name as an exact fix.",
            when Catalogue.Stray_Token =>
               "A run of tokens begins no declaration or statement [1740"
               & "]. Often a keyword used as a name (D225), or a line left"
               & " from an edit. A `fixed if` inside a routine body is one"
               & " too: it selects module declarations [1500], so declare "
               & "a routine per system in a module-level `fixed if`, or br"
               & "anch with `if` on a module value that holds the fact, `o"
               & "n_linux: bool = compiler.os == linux` (D437).",
            when Catalogue.Nesting_Too_Deep =>
               "An implementation limit, not a rule of the language: a c"
               & "onstruct nests more deeply than the parser holds. Split "
               & "the expression or the block into named parts.",
            when Catalogue.Positional_After_Named =>
               "A positional argument follows a named one [0980]. Every "
               & "positional argument comes first.",
            when Catalogue.Duplicate_Declaration =>
               "One scope gives one name to one thing [1850]. Two declar"
               & "ations of one name in one scope, or two imports with one"
               & " final segment, are refused, and the second label shows "
               & "the first. An inner scope may shadow an outer name; that"
               & " is not this.",
            when Catalogue.Unresolved_Name =>
               "A name that is declared in no scope this use reaches [18"
               & "60]. There is no implicit declaration, so it is a misspe"
               & "lling or a name used outside its scope. When a declared "
               & "name the position could mean is near it, the diagnostic "
               & "offers that name as a likely fix: a local or parameter, "
               & "a type, a public member of an imported module, never a n"
               & "ame out of scope or inaccessible. A member a module decl"
               & "ares only in a `fixed if` arm this target does not selec"
               & "t, a Linux call written for Darwin among them, is named "
               & "as one this system does not have, since no spelling of i"
               & "t would be found here."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "A name applied to type arguments, `shlf(item)`, is the s"
               & "ame misspelling and is offered the same near names. A pa"
               & "yload-free case of a variant another module declares is "
               & "written with that module's name, as everything public in"
               & " it is [1440], so a bare `leaf` naming an imported modul"
               & "e's case is offered `shapes.leaf`. A scalar type written"
               & " as a positional argument of a generic routine is a type"
               & " where a value belongs; the note writes the call with ev"
               & "ery argument named, the type given to the routine's type"
               & " formal [1300], as `make_buffer(capacity: 4, t: u8)`."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "A parameter, result or local may hide an import of its o"
               & "wn name [1450], so `time.duration` written where a resul"
               & "t is called `time` names no type. The diagnostic says so"
               & ", names the local and the import it hides, and points at"
               & " the local; rename it (D381).",
            when Catalogue.Inaccessible_Name =>
               "A declaration of another module is used and it is not `p"
               & "ublic` [1410]. The second label shows the declaration. M"
               & "ake it `public` in its module, or use something that mod"
               & "ule does export. A module-internal type's member that is"
               & " an entry of a concept the type conforms to is reached t"
               & "hrough the public routine of the concept's module that c"
               & "alls it [1240], and the note names that routine as this "
               & "file calls it: `memory.alloc(64, 1)` on a `hosted/heap` "
               & "handle is `mem.allocate(memory, ...)`.",
            when Catalogue.Reserved_Tool_Name =>
               "A tool namespace, `compiler`, `assembler` or `linker`, i"
               & "s bound or used in a way it does not allow [1560] (D202)"
               & ". Those three are in scope without an import and cannot "
               & "be imported, rebound or given a member they do not have."
               & " A compiler fact is read in a fixed condition and in a m"
               & "odule value (D437), never in a routine body: bind it, `f"
               & "ast: bool = compiler.feature.popcnt`, and let the body r"
               & "ead the binding. `compiler.os` and the other atom facts "
               & "are read compared with one of their atoms, `compiler.os "
               & "== linux`.",
            when Catalogue.Literal_Out_Of_Range =>
               "A value known at compile time does not fit the type its "
               & "context gives it [1880], or the target cannot hold it. W"
               & "rite a smaller value or give the context a wider type.",
            when Catalogue.Register_Reserved_Bits =>
               "A register image known at compile time violates its rese"
               & "rved-bit write policy [0740] (D228). Supply zero in ever"
               & "y unnamed bit for `write_zero`, or one in every unnamed "
               & "bit for `write_one`. A whole-image write cannot repair t"
               & "hose bits by reading the device. The image may fit its c"
               & "arrier type; L0300 instead reports a value that its type"
               & " or target cannot hold.",
            when Catalogue.Type_Mismatch =>
               "A value's type is not the one its context or operation r"
               & "equires [1890], and no conversion is implied [0310]. Thi"
               & "s includes a literal that its context cannot type [1880]"
               & " [0210] [0260], an expression with no value type where o"
               & "ne is needed, a type-qualified name its type does not ha"
               & "ve [0240], an operation such as indexing, slicing, selec"
               & "tion or a call applied to a value whose type has none [1"
               & "820], an operator given an operand class it does not adm"
               & "it, a struct of another nominal type [0710], an array of"
               & " another length or element type, a function of another s"
               & "ignature [1000], or a reference of another permission [0"
               & "440]. The second label shows where the requirement was s"
               & "tated. Change the value, or convert it explicitly where "
               & "a conversion exists. A text literal takes `utf8`, `[]u8`"
               & ", `utf16` or `cstring` from its context but never a poin"
               & "ter; for a `ptr u8` parameter, bind it, `name: []u8 = ""."
               & "..""`, and pass `addr name[0]`, since the literal ends in"
               & " NUL (D442).",
            when Catalogue.Not_Definitely_Assigned =>
               "Required storage is not definitely assigned at a read or"
               & " an exit [1910]. A read needs the place assigned on ever"
               & "y path that reaches it. Reading a whole aggregate also r"
               & "eads its parts; a computed local-array index requires th"
               & "e whole array assigned (D19-D22). Assign the needed plac"
               & "e before the read on every arriving path, or give it a v"
               & "alue where it is declared."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "After `sink`, the consumed place is dead until assigned "
               & "again [0910]. Assign it or its enclosing aggregate befor"
               & "e a later read. A consumed part of an `inout` parameter "
               & "must also be restored on every exit, including `fail` an"
               & "d `try` failure propagation: the caller can observe that"
               & " storage after a recovered failure. Assign it on each ex"
               & "it path, either before the exit or in an applicable `def"
               & "er` or `undo` cleanup, which runs before this check. A n"
               & "amed result must be fully assigned on successful return "
               & "[0930], including any part consumed by `sink`; failure e"
               & "xits do not require the named result.",
            when Catalogue.Immutable_Target =>
               "A place that may not be written [1900]: an immutable bin"
               & "ding, an `in` parameter, an atom, a function, or storage"
               & " reached through a read-only reference. When the place i"
               & "s a local or module binding of one name, the diagnostic "
               & "offers `mut` on its declaration as a likely fix. A bindi"
               & "ng written several times is reported once, at its first "
               & "write, and a refused write still counts as assigning the"
               & " place, so later reads are not reported (D263).",
            when Catalogue.Unsupported_Use =>
               "A known form used where the language does not permit it "
               & "[1830], found once the checker knows what the form means"
               & ". The report names the specific rule; its two notes give"
               & " the tour paragraph and the form's standing."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "For a variant [0680]-[0690] (D75/D76/D241), its part bel"
               & "ongs to the enclosing struct and has no standalone value"
               & ". Match the part to inspect its case, or copy the whole "
               & "struct. To change the part, write one of its cases to a "
               & "directly selected part of a mutable struct, or supply th"
               & "at case while constructing the struct. A case cannot ini"
               & "tialize an unrelated binding as a standalone value: its "
               & "destination must supply its variant part. A case without"
               & " payload may be bare; write a payload case with labelled"
               & " fields."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "An array literal [0520] takes its shape from where it is"
               & " written: an array destination, an inferred binding, or "
               & "the argument of a read-only slice parameter, which it le"
               & "nds a slice of storage made in the caller's frame for th"
               & "e call. A generic routine's slice parameter gives one on"
               & "ly when its element type names no formal (D419); where t"
               & "he element type is a formal, deduced from the arguments,"
               & " the report names the binding to pass instead, `values :"
               & "= [...]`, or `values: [N]E = [...]` when an element such"
               & " as `any(addr x)` needs a context, which an inferred bin"
               & "ding does not give.",
            when Catalogue.Not_Known_At_Compile_Time =>
               "A required static value or initial image cannot be estab"
               & "lished before the program runs [1940] (D136, D202). A mo"
               & "dule value, array bound or fixed configuration expressio"
               & "n can depend on a runtime value or call, contain an unkn"
               & "own fixed name or form, or depend on itself, within one "
               & "module or through several. A fixed condition or option d"
               & "efault measures scalar types only: a declared type's siz"
               & "e, alignment or field offset is measured by `compiler.as"
               & "sert`, once checking has laid the type out (D412). An ar"
               & "ray bound may name an immutable module integer whose own"
               & " image is a count, literals, compiler facts and other su"
               & "ch integers under `+ - * / %`, but not a `mut` one, whic"
               & "h the program may write (D438). Change such an expressio"
               & "n to one the closed fold can evaluate. A value another m"
               & "odule exports, named through that module as `sizes.page`"
               & ", is known as it is in its own module; a field of a reco"
               & "rd image, an element of an array image and a call are no"
               & "t, in either. A module function binding without an initi"
               & "alizer has no implicit zero function address; give it an"
               & " initial function address, such as a declared function o"
               & "r another module function value whose image is known.",
            when Catalogue.Impossible_Operand =>
               "An operand the operation cannot take, where the compiler"
               & " knows it [1950]: a divisor of zero, a shift by a negati"
               & "ve amount, an index outside a fixed array, or a range su"
               & "btype whose bounds are reversed.",
            when Catalogue.Compile_Time_Assertion_Failed =>
               "A compile-time assertion is false [1510].",
            when Catalogue.Cyclic_Type_Alias =>
               "A chain of type aliases that never reaches a type [1795]"
               & ".",
            when Catalogue.Unresolved_Field =>
               "A field a struct, a variant case or a result was not dec"
               & "lared with [0750] [0990]. When a declared field is near "
               & "the written name, the diagnostic offers it as a likely f"
               & "ix.",
            when Catalogue.Field_Named_Twice =>
               "A struct declaration [0670] or literal [0710] repeats a "
               & "field name, a variant case declaration [0680] (D74) repe"
               & "ats a payload field name, or a case construction (D76) s"
               & "upplies the same payload field twice. Remove or rename a"
               & " repeated declaration field; in a literal or constructio"
               & "n, supply each field once."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "For a case declared as `pair: (first: u8, second: bool)`"
               & ", the construction `pair(first: 1, first: 2, second: tru"
               & "e)` repeats `first`.",
            when Catalogue.Field_Not_Given =>
               "A struct literal [0710] or variant case construction (D7"
               & "6) omits a field without a trailing `of zeroed`. Supply "
               & "the missing field, or use `of zeroed` when every omitted"
               & " field has a zero image."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "For a case declared as `pair: (first: u8, second: bool)`"
               & ", the construction `pair(first: 1)` omits `second`.",
            when Catalogue.Variant_Case_Named_Twice =>
               "A match names one case twice [1210]: a variant case, an "
               & "atom of a set or a pointer union's case, twice in one ar"
               & "m or once in each of two (D405). Keep one label and dele"
               & "te the other.",
            when Catalogue.Variant_Case_Not_Matched =>
               "A match leaves a case unnamed [1210]. For a variant part"
               & ", add an arm naming each missing case. For an atom set o"
               & "r pointer union, name the missing cases or put a `_:` ar"
               & "m last to cover them.",
            when Catalogue.Recursive_Nominal_Value =>
               "A struct holds itself by value, so its layout could neve"
               & "r be finite (D137). Hold it through a pointer.",
            when Catalogue.Reference_Escapes =>
               "Retaining a reference requires both storage that remains"
               & " live and permission from its origin [0770] [0780]. A re"
               & "ference into this function's frame cannot be returned, p"
               & "assed to a retaining (`escaping`) parameter, or stored o"
               & "utside the frame. Move the referenced value to storage t"
               & "hat actually outlives the retention, or stop retaining t"
               & "he reference. Declaring a parameter `escaping` does not "
               & "extend the lifetime of frame storage."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "Parameters are non-escaping by default. A reference deri"
               & "ved from one cannot be passed to a retaining (`escaping`"
               & ") call or stored in another origin, even if the referenc"
               & "ed storage will remain live. If that retention is intend"
               & "ed, declare the source parameter `escaping`, or `escapin"
               & "g into` the parameter whose storage keeps it (D445), and"
               & " make its callers satisfy that contract. A reference kep"
               & "t `escaping into` a parameter must outlive that argument"
               & "'s origin: a frame reference never outlives a parameter'"
               & "s storage, and a local only the storage of locals declar"
               & "ed after it (D455). Otherwise, keep the use non-retainin"
               & "g or update storage within the same origin. Keeping the "
               & "storage alive longer alone does not grant retention perm"
               & "ission.",
            when Catalogue.Borrowed_Place =>
               "A place is changed while a view derived from it is still"
               & " in use [0800] [0830]. Finish with the view first, or ta"
               & "ke it again after the change. An argument passed `inout`"
               & " or `sink` counts as changed whether or not the routine "
